+Keep one authoritative board per event. Editors submit commands over HTTPS; the server assigns each committed edit one event revision. The server delivers committed revisions to browsers over self-hosted WebSocket connections: it holds a persistent connection per browser, publishes each new revision to the connections subscribed to that event, and browsers apply revisions in order. Subsecond updates would be useful but are not required; the 15-second freshness target governs.
 
