+
+- The change store retains an ordered, replayable revision history and reliably hands each committed revision to delivery for publication.
+- Delivery owns the WebSocket sessions — accepting and tracking connections and publishing each revision to its subscribers.
+- Browser sync subscribes over a WebSocket, treats a dropped connection as a visible stale state, and catches up on revisions missed while disconnected.
 
